@baseUrl = http://localhost:5000

### register (employee). The password must be 12-72 characters (a short one -> 400)
POST {{baseUrl}}/auth/users
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "firstName": "Test",
  "lastName": "User",
  "email": "testuser@sdp.test",
  "password": "A-long-password-123",
  "department": "PASTE_ENG_DEPARTMENT_ID"
}

### login as seeded employee
# @name login
POST {{baseUrl}}/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "employee@sdp.test",
  "password": "Passw0rd!"
}

### check-auth (cookie sent automatically by the REST client)
GET {{baseUrl}}/auth/check-auth

### logout (POST; the old GET /auth/logout is now 404)
POST {{baseUrl}}/auth/logout

### logout with GET -> 404 (it was a GET before HARDENING)
GET {{baseUrl}}/auth/logout

### register is rate limited: more than 10/hour per IP -> 429
### register needs a BUSINESS department (an IT_SUPPORT department id -> 400)
POST {{baseUrl}}/auth/users
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "firstName": "Bad",
  "lastName": "Dept",
  "email": "baddept@sdp.test",
  "password": "Passw0rd!",
  "department": "PASTE_IT_SUPPORT_DEPARTMENT_ID"
}

### wrong password 10 times in 15 min -> 429 (successful logins are not counted)
POST {{baseUrl}}/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{ "email": "employee@sdp.test", "password": "wrong" }

### change password (use this on the live admin after the first seed)
PUT {{baseUrl}}/auth/password
Content-Type: application/json

{ "currentPassword": "Passw0rd!", "newPassword": "A-much-longer-new-password-1" }

### health: db, cron and version (no login). Live: https://<vercel-app>/api/health
GET {{baseUrl}}/health

### change password: new password must be 12-72 characters -> 400 otherwise
PUT {{baseUrl}}/auth/password
Content-Type: application/json

{ "currentPassword": "Passw0rd!", "newPassword": "short" }

### the same account is also limited per email: 20 wrong passwords in 15 minutes -> 429
### (even from different IP addresses), on top of the 10-per-IP limit above

### HARDENING: malformed JSON -> 400 {"error":"invalid JSON body"} (it used to be a 500)
POST {{baseUrl}}/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{"email": 

### HARDENING: registering an email that already exists -> 409 "email already exists" (the address itself is not echoed back)
POST {{baseUrl}}/auth/users
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "firstName": "Dup",
  "email": "employee@sdp.test",
  "password": "A-long-password-123",
  "department": "PASTE_ENG_DEPARTMENT_ID"
}

### HARDENING: an unknown id in a path -> 400 "invalid id" (not 500)
GET {{baseUrl}}/ticket-api/tickets/not-a-valid-id

### HARDENING: sessions
# 1. log in twice (two REST client windows, or one browser + one REST client)
# 2. in one of them: PUT /auth/password with a valid new password -> 200
# 3. in the OTHER one: GET /auth/check-auth -> 401 "Session expired, please login again"
# 4. log in again with the new password -> 200 and check-auth works
# (tokens carry whole seconds, so wait a second between step 1 and step 2)
# The auth cookie now lives as long as JWT_EXPIRES_IN (default 1d): look at Max-Age in the Set-Cookie of the login response
